      "content": "i hear you on the civilian impact, but you're saying \"nuanced thesis\" and \"trade-off,\" but you've mostly just pointed out why sanctions fail or are unethical. if i'm being honest, it feels like you're saying sanctions are basically just a failed, immoral policy. aren't there cases where they actually work? or are you saying they're just fundamentally a bad idea across the board?",
